{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/948499-how-do-you-challenge-your-players-with-puzzles","id":948499,"title":"How do you challenge your players with puzzles?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-11T04:15:37-07:00","id":948499,"title":"How do you challenge your players with puzzles?","content":"I have a short game on the horizon that is essentially a supplementary story to the long form games we have been running over the last 5 years. <br /> <br /> We run all of our games in a concurrent universe where all games are on the same continuum and actions in one story will echo into another one. The main villain from the very first game TPK'd the party and her name has been synonymous with WoD evil ever since. <br /> <br /> I have asked the players to pick their favourite characters from 5 years worth of games and prepare them to go on the final hunt. We now have party mainly of Mages, with one Vampire and one Werewolf making up the rest of the party. The enemy is an ancient Baali, powerful and dangerous she is not afraid to flaunt her abilities.<br /> <br /> Whilst I intend this to be a fast game, I don't just want it to be a combat dominated slog like previous games of this ilk have been.<br /> <br /> My question to you is;<b> how have you integrated puzzles into a WoD setting</b>? What type of puzzles have you run and how successful were they? <br /> <br /> Thanks very much,<br /> <br /> Saul","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;One half tender, one half <i>tenderize&quot;.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3107-saul-of-tarsus","name":"Saul of Tarsus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T10:52:11-07:00","id":948692,"title":"","content":"The one thing to be aware of with puzzles is what may seem like an easy puzzle to you might not be apparent to the players. The players shouldn't be punished for 'not getting' the puzzle when their characters should, so one bit of advice I would offer is allow your players to make appropriate rolls to get hints on the solution to a puzzle. What they roll would be based on the type of puzzle and the way it works, so for example a mathematical puzzle might have Perception + Academics (to notice the numerical pattern) or Intelligence + Academics (to solve the equations). Basically if it seems like your players are floundering badly or they ask if they can have their characters traits come into play, let them. Nothing is more frustrating than not being able to 'figure out' a puzzle as a player and basically being stuck when your character should be able to figure it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T11:15:59-07:00","id":948709,"title":"","content":"While Im thinking about it make sure to tie the puzzles to the character using them. So using your ancient Baali here are some example puzzles<ul><li>A mathematics puzzle based around the work of an ancient mathematician</li> <li>A puzzle where the characters have to play the part in an ancient story or play. Example: The players come across a room full of statues (or fleshcrafted corpses, mannequins, etc.) put in positions and dressed as if they were in the battle of Troy. The doorway out is magically locked and the key is somewhere among the 'scenery'. One answer could be a rune carefully placed on the achilles tendon of Achilles.</li> <li>A stage where the characters have to act out the temptation of Eve by the Serpent in the Garden of Eden.</li> <li>A logic puzzle using the names of various infernal entities as the blocks and the characters have to set them in the correct order (which could be by importance, alphabet, religion of origin, etc)</li> <li>The Baali has placed a preserved sample of an ancient and terrible disease (possibly altered by Baali Dark Thaumaturgy) (some examples smallpox, the plague of Athens, the plague of Justinian, typhus, cholera) that the characters have to locate before it is released and ravages a population, the puzzle is a map with locations listed from a famous ancient journey (some examples the Odyssey, Hercules's 12 labors)</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T03:41:01-07:00","id":949221,"title":"","content":"Hey Cynic, thanks so much for your responses. Your bulletpoint list is really interesting and those are very unique ideas of puzzles, thanks so much for your input! <br /> <br /> As far as your first piece of advice goes, it is a very good one. When doing puzzles I like to keep a few solutions in mind normally, and will often accept a solution that perhaps I hadn't thought of but is flavourful enough to be the correct answer. Puzzles are tough but I appreciate you giving me a hand on this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;One half tender, one half <i>tenderize&quot;.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3107-saul-of-tarsus","name":"Saul of Tarsus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:31:52-07:00","id":949395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saul of Tarsus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/948499-how-do-you-challenge-your-players-with-puzzles?p=949221#post949221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Cynic, thanks so much for your responses. Your bulletpoint list is really interesting and those are very unique ideas of puzzles, thanks so much for your input!<br /> <br /> As far as your first piece of advice goes, it is a very good one. When doing puzzles I like to keep a few solutions in mind normally, and will often accept a solution that perhaps I hadn't thought of but is flavourful enough to be the correct answer. Puzzles are tough but I appreciate you giving me a hand on this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad I could help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T13:19:15-07:00","id":949491,"title":"","content":"Several years back on of our Bigger Interactive missions had a table trying to hack in to a large star base controlled by the imperials Inquisitor group (Force hunters), so we could try and locate some captured jedi.. The DM who wrote it, had it based off Sodoku, with 3 separate levels.. Pcs could roll an appropriate skill to get a hint (or three), but it was on THEM (the player) to solve it not just rely on dice rolling..<br /> However he DID iirc have a rule in there which if that was how they wanted to do it, Roll it out rather than solve it out... They could, but it would be a series of Contested rolls of THEIR computer skill vs the enemy &quot;Lan administrator&quot; skill... 3 straight successes were needed to break through. If the enemy got 3 straight, the pcs were perma locked out..<br /> <br /> However, i always like doing it if you ARE going to give the puzzle to the Players to solve, make it a TIMED evolution.. However long they take IRL to solve it is how long their 'character's took IN GAME to solve it....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}